  ('cd29ff92-27bd-4c7e-8e92-124156e1f540', '598c5fb5-bf93-47fe-b9d3-144c4c41b93a', $q$Fixed price$q$, $q$Fixed$q$, 15, 60);
insert into interventions (id, template_id, key, name, year, recipients, subject, message, photo_path, depends_on) values
  ('4843b962-9e08-43ca-9de5-09366ccb37af', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$3_csr_infrastructure_development$q$, $q$3 CSR - Infrastructure development$q$, 18, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Investment Proposal - Infrastructure Development$q$, $q$<p>You have received several proposals for investment programs in local infrastructure:</p><p><br></p><p><strong>1. Long-term Infrastructure Projects</strong></p><p>Support major infrastructure improvements - such as roads and bridges - to benefit both energy developments and local communities.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>2. Electrification Program</strong></p><p>Provide electricity to rural communities through solar mini-grids, with plans to connect them to the national grid. Program managed by Melhuana Katanya, VP at Southern Grid Company.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>3. Relocation and Infrastructure for Fishing Villages</strong></p><p>Relocate fishing villages to enable supplier industry expansion. The project includes new housing, infrastructure, education, and transitional financial support.</p>$q$, $q$photos/4843b962-9e08-43ca-9de5-09366ccb37af.jpg$q$, '{}'::text[]),
  ('2e62eb17-e341-44ac-bf2a-ac976cc68c10', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2042_lcoe_update$q$, $q$2042 LCOE Update$q$, 17, $q$ALL$q$, $q$LCOE Update 2042$q$, $q$<ul><li>Renewables are mature and flexibility drives value.</li><li><strong>Solar</strong> and <strong>onshore wind</strong> still improve, but grid position, financing, and delivery speed matter most.</li><li><strong>Bottom fixed offshore wind</strong> is firmly established.</li><li><strong>Floating offshore wind</strong> has scaled through standard platforms and more efficient offshore operations.</li><li><strong>Batteries</strong> are core infrastructure now - reducing curtailment and boosting firm delivery in a variable power system. </li></ul>$q$, $q$photos/2e62eb17-e341-44ac-bf2a-ac976cc68c10.jpg$q$, '{}'::text[]),
  ('84d4dbd8-4a97-4f7c-a72b-989d840f4e5a', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2_csr_health_programs$q$, $q$2 CSR - Health Programs$q$, 11, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Investment Proposal - Health Programs$q$, $q$<p>You have received several proposals for health-focused social investments:</p><p><br></p><p><strong>1. Malaria Control Program</strong></p><p>A program to prevent and treat malaria through insecticide-treated bed nets and training for local healthcare workers.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>2. Safe Drinking Water Project</strong></p><p>A project addressing unsafe drinking water in both peri-urban and rural areas. It includes drilling for clean water, improving existing reservoirs, and aims to reduce rural-to-urban migration.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>3. Mobile Medical Units</strong></p><p>A proposal from a key business partner of Exlandian Oil Company to build mobile medical units for remote villages. Each unit costs $1 million, plus $800,000 per year in operating expenses.</p>$q$, $q$photos/84d4dbd8-4a97-4f7c-a72b-989d840f4e5a.jpg$q$, '{}'::text[]),
  ('9f868e0d-a88e-4a1a-a2a1-7f34d8a24af0', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2035_lcoe_update$q$, $q$2035 - LCOE Update$q$, 10, $q$ALL$q$, $q$LCOE Update 2035$q$, $q$<ul><li>Costs keep falling, but execution becomes the real differentiator.</li><li><strong>Solar</strong> and <strong>onshore wind</strong> continue downward through reliability and O&amp;M gains.</li><li><strong>Bottom fixed offshore wind</strong> becomes more competitive with larger turbines and more industrialised supply chains.</li><li><strong>Floating offshore wind</strong> begins scaling beyond pilots.</li><li><strong>Batteries</strong> get cheaper per delivered MWh as cycle life improves - making storage a strategic portfolio tool.</li></ul>$q$, $q$photos/9f868e0d-a88e-4a1a-a2a1-7f34d8a24af0.jpg$q$, '{}'::text[]),
  ('7f7d3b29-fc46-4756-bd97-5c33cc2560b2', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$csr_higher_education$q$, $q$CSR - Higher Education$q$, 7, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Investment Proposal - Higher Education$q$, $q$<p>You have received several proposals for social investment programs in the education sector:</p><p><br></p><p><strong>1. "You Company" Scholarship Scheme</strong></p><p>A long-term program offering scholarships for students from host communities to pursue higher education.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>2. Global Scholarship Project</strong></p><p>Funding for talented individuals from Port Royal to study at Ivy League universities. The initiative is led by Swift Taylor, wife of Sam Taylor, an executive at Exlandian Oil Company.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>3. National Teacher Upskilling Project</strong></p><p>A national effort to strengthen local content by increasing the number of skilled engineers. The project aims to improve elementary education by doubling the number of high school science teachers.</p>$q$, $q$photos/7f7d3b29-fc46-4756-bd97-5c33cc2560b2.jpg$q$, '{}'::text[]),
  ('b554fe48-d42a-4234-bd23-c4702ba5311d', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2030_lcoe_update$q$, $q$2030 - LCOE Update$q$, 4, $q$ALL$q$, $q$LCOE Update 2030$q$, $q$<ul><li><strong>Utility solar</strong> and <strong>onshore wind</strong> are now the cheapest new-build options in many markets, driven by better performance and faster, more standardised build-out.</li><li><strong>Bottom fixed offshore wind</strong> is improving, but still pricier.</li><li><strong>Batteries</strong> are shifting from "nice-to-have" to a normal part of project design as lifetime and efficiency improve - though grid access is becoming a key constraint.</li></ul>$q$, $q$photos/b554fe48-d42a-4234-bd23-c4702ba5311d.jpg$q$, '{}'::text[]),
  ('80965491-e911-40c3-85ae-f8dbdfa41d60', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2046_energy_update$q$, $q$2046 - Energy Update$q$, 20, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Energy Update 2045$q$, $q$<p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">The net-zero emissions policy is now being implemented globally.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">All oil and gas producers are now held responsible for level 2 and level 3 emissions.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">The Exlandian government expects all parties in the fossil fuel value chain to comply.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">CO2 tax is increasing to $300 per ton, and taxes are raised with 5% on oil and gas activities.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">CO2 tax set to $300/tonnes</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Offshore tax set to 65%</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Onshore tax set to 45%</strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('edeb7952-24b4-4421-9a58-42211d630078', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2041_energy_update$q$, $q$2041 - Energy Update$q$, 16, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Energy Update 2041$q$, $q$<p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">In response to growing global pressure to reduce CO2 emissions and contribute to a sustainable future, Exlandia is implementing policy changes in line with its commitment to achieve net-zero emissions by 2050.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">CO2 tax is increasing to $200 per ton. In addition, the government is introducing a negative tax on renewable energy projects.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">CO2 tax set to $200/tonnes</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Renewable tax set to -15%</strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('081af6d2-86b9-47a5-8ff5-98067d6c57c8', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2031_electrification_law_on_fossil_fuel_assets$q$, $q$2031 - Electrification Law on Fossil Fuel Assets$q$, 6, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Electrification Law on Fossil Fuel Assets$q$, $q$<p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Exlandia has passed a new Electrification Law requiring energy companies to eliminate emissions from all fossil fuel producing assets, including midstream operations.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">To comply, energy producers must invest in new renewable electricity assets. You need to return as much electricity to the grid as you consume for production in order to maintain a steady energy supply to Exlandia.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><em>Further details on how this law affects specific assets will be provided soon.&nbsp;</em></strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('4fbbf274-195f-49a5-80a6-ba8abfe603ab', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2030_energy_update$q$, $q$2030 - Energy Update$q$, 5, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Energy Update 2030$q$, $q$<p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">In line with the country’s commitment to achieve net-zero emissions by 2050, Exlandia is increasing CO2 tax to $100 per ton.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">CO2 tax set to $100/tonnes</strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('c92a1abd-e24b-4b79-bfad-398916043dac', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2026_energy_update$q$, $q$2026 - Energy Update$q$, 1, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Energy Update 2026$q$, $q$<p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">The coal production in Exlandia is declining according to plan. From its peak of 20 million tons in 2020, it now represents less than 30% of energy demand. This shift is driven by the acceleration of oil and gas production.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">To further support the energy transition, Exlandia is increasing CO2 tax to $70 per ton.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">CO2 tax set to $70/tonnes</strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('c2c55b84-c021-497f-af45-23429636b0d7', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2031_electrification$q$, $q$2031 Electrification$q$, null, $q$ALL$q$, $q$"Electrification Law on Fossil Fuels Producers and mid-stream assets"$q$, $q$<p>The Law just sanctioned requires that all mentioned must comply by 2033. This encompasses measures to remove emissions from producing assets and assets using fossil fuels for mid-stream activities.</p><p>In addition to invest in electrification, it is mandatory to invest in renewable assets to add energy in Mwh to the Exlandian grid that compensates for the energy needed for electrification. This Law shall not decrease capacity for the land of Exlandia.</p><p>The government trusts that companies involved in the afore mentioned activities knows the energy needed to replace gas turbines and therefor the renewable capacity needed to compensate for their electrification project.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>It is expected that all parties convene, as appropriate, to conclude on electrification and renewable investments. </em></strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('1fc47560-b575-46b9-a6b8-eab058bfb151', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2046_update_on_energy_climate_and_fiscal_regime$q$, $q$2046 Update on Energy, Climate and Fiscal regime$q$, null, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Update on Energy, Climate and Fiscal regime - MAJOR CHANGES IN FISCAL REGIME$q$, $q$<p>The 0 emissions policy is now being implemented globally and supported by the Exlandian government. All oil and gas producers are now held responsible for level 2 and level 3 emissions and taxed accordingly.</p><p>This will imply major impact on all upstream, midstream and consumption on fossil fuels.</p><p>The government expects all parties in the fossil fuels value chains to join forces to ensure 0 emission is accomplished.</p><p><span style="color: black;">To ensure that a balance is established and that oil and gas producers are leading this initiative an extra tax, without affecting the depreciation cash reduction, is effective immediately.</span></p><p><strong style="color: black;">The CO2 tax is increased to $500 per ton. Income tax is increased by 5 p.p. for oil and gas (now 65% / 45%).</strong></p><p><strong style="color: black;"><em>Energy companies are strongly advised to evaluate climate changes and fiscal regime impact on business.</em></strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('0cc8da6c-2a8a-485d-98a8-e46a08ed0b1c', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2041_update_on_energy_climate_and_fiscal_regime$q$, $q$2041 Update on Energy, Climate and Fiscal regime$q$, null, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Update on Energy, Climate and Fiscal regime$q$, $q$<p>Climate update: IEA forecasts Global warming to surpass 3,3% for 2050.</p><p>In Exlandia, level 3 or 4 hurricanes implies major threat to offshore facilities. Lethal heath during summer is considered a threat while rain is new to dominate the usually dry winter seasons. The wind is still increasing turning towards north and increases is strength. The central parts of Exlandia is becoming more inhabitable.</p><p><span style="color: black;">Additional measures are needed to realize the energy transition. CO2 tax is increased and implemented for all emitting assets. The support for renewables and low carbon solutions are increased.</span></p><p><strong style="color: black;">The CO2 tax is increased to $400 per ton. Income tax is decreased with additional -5 p.p for renewables (to -15%).</strong></p><p><strong style="color: black;"><em>Energy companies are strongly advised to evaluate climate changes and fiscal regime impact on business.</em></strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('623cb625-de05-4fa3-98a7-3761bea07f01', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2034_update_on_energy_climate_and_fiscal_regime$q$, $q$2034 Update on Energy, Climate and Fiscal regime$q$, null, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Update on Energy, Climate and Fiscal regime - MAJOR TAX ADJUSTMENTS$q$, $q$<p><span style="color: black;">Climate update: IEA forecasts Global warming to exceed 2,8 degrees by 2050.</span></p><p><span style="color: black;">﻿In Exlandia, the weather pattern continues to challenge the energy sector. Wind is increasing and rapidly shifting from west to north. The effect is more rain in the central and changed conditions for both wind and solar projects. 2035 is expected to be the worst hurricane season ever.</span></p><p><span style="color: black;">To support global initiatives and mitigate emissions the government has decided to increase the CO2 tax to $300 per ton, while using tax to provide support-prices for renewable energy production and CCS. The Tax regime for all emitting assets in the hydrocarbon sector is increased to 60% for offshore and 40% for onshore, while renewables are provided with 10% tax deduction to support investments.</span></p><p><strong style="color: black;">The CO2 tax is increased to $300 per ton. Income tax is increased by 10 p.p. for oil and gas, -10 p.p for renewables.</strong></p><p><strong style="color: black;"><em>Energy companies are strongly advised to evaluate climate changes and fiscal regime impact on business.</em></strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('5532ee38-9b7b-40e0-a1cf-ad429e1f727b', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2030_update_on_energy_climate_and_fiscal_regime$q$, $q$2030 Update on Energy, Climate and Fiscal regime$q$, null, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Update on Energy, Climate and Fiscal regime $q$, $q$<p><strong>Climate update: I</strong>EA forecasts Global warming to 2,6% 2050.</p><p>There are changes in wind patterns across Exlandia. In the northern part there are hurricanes, level 2, impacting all installations. Sandstorms creates major impact on livelihood and facilities in all central parts. The average temperature is rapidly increasing in central Exlandia.</p><p><span style="color: black;">On average the temperature is forecasted to increase by 5-7 degrees by 2035.</span></p><p><strong style="color: black;">The CO2 tax is increased to $200 per ton. </strong></p><p><strong style="color: black;"><em>Energy companies are strongly advised to evaluate climate changes and fiscal regime impact on business.</em></strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('d4b19528-e2d9-42ee-8e5a-99419caf2f32', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$2026_update_on_energy_climate_and_fiscal_regime$q$, $q$2026 Update on Energy, Climate and Fiscal regime$q$, null, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Update on Energy, Climate and Fiscal regime$q$, $q$<p>The coal production in Exlandia is reduced according to plan. From its peak of 20 million tons in 2020, it presently represents less than 30% of energy demand. The shift is driven by transition to oil and gas.</p><p>To strengthen the energy transition the government increases the CO2 tax to $ 100 per ton. The tax will be used to subsidize development of renewables and low carbon solution.</p><p><strong>CO2 tax has been set to $100 per ton, effective as of January 1, 2027</strong></p><p><strong style="color: black;"><em>Energy companies are strongly advised to evaluate climate changes and fiscal regime impact on business.</em></strong></p>$q$, null, '{}'::text[]),
  ('57c97040-9cca-412f-b22b-7693ea425b4d', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', $q$increased_investment_in_reneawble_energy$q$, $q$increased_investment_in_reneawble_energy? $q$, null, $q$ALL$q$, $q$Increased investment in reneawble energy?$q$, $q$
