  ('81a35c28-5a41-4a37-b12c-6280a4d8d9c7', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', '280c25c1-e370-473c-9da0-cfacda8a4a35', $q$Luna$q$, $q$1Tie_in_Luna-Luna$q$, 2, $q$LUNA - Prospect drilled successfully$q$, $q$<p>Exploration has confirmed a discovery of 79 million barrels (Mbbl) of oil and 9 MSm3 gas within the licence area, located 12 kilometers from Luna. </p><p><br></p><p>Two development options are being considered.</p>$q$, $q$1. Accelerated development, oil in 2 years, estimated CAPEX 710 MUSD.$q$, null, true, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('22ef9fa7-7eb7-49b3-bab3-a50bceb4511f', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', 'e40fcdf7-31b9-4b9b-8cff-e924d0cc49e5', $q$Amura$q$, $q$2AmuraTie_in-Amura$q$, 2, $q$$q$, $q$$q$, $q$2. Further prospect evaluations to refine the business case, estimated CAPEX is 560 MUSD, first oil in 4 years.$q$, null, true, null, null, $q$offshore$q$, true, 0, true, null),
  ('ca5dd82a-9c56-4f2a-bd11-146c4e62e627', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', 'e40fcdf7-31b9-4b9b-8cff-e924d0cc49e5', $q$Amura$q$, $q$1AmuraTie_in-Amura$q$, 2, $q$AMURA - Prospect drilled successfully$q$, $q$<p>Exploration has confirmed a discovery of 70 million barrels (mmbbl) of oil and 9 MSm3 gas within the licence area, located 12 kilometers from Amura.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Two development options are being considered.</strong></p>$q$, $q$1. Accelerated development, oil in 2 years, estimated CAPEX of 710 million MUSD.$q$, null, true, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('083c5a72-8f60-483a-933c-32726a2f625b', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', 'e38e608a-4b65-409d-ab70-be7dc51e5f8f', $q$Aurelia$q$, $q$Y1_2Aurelia_new field design_NO-Aurelia$q$, 3, $q$$q$, $q$$q$, $q$2. Stick to the original field development plan.$q$, null, true, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('da37c44a-9285-4975-af50-f778dbed6cc4', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', '3d954298-e0c2-4a9f-ad33-dc557f0f74b1', $q$Breeze$q$, $q$1 Community resistance$q$, 3, $q$Breeze Offshore Wind - Local Fishing Community Resistance$q$, $q$<p>A local fishing community is protesting your wind farm project, claiming it disrupts their fishing grounds. They are threating to involve the government, and are demanding compensation and environmental studies to protect marine life.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>All production has been stopped until mitigating action is in place.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>You have two options for mitigation:</p>$q$, $q$1. Initiate negotiations for compensation package. Increases remaining CAPEX with $0.5 M/MW, and delays the project with 2 years.$q$, null, null, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('c8bb6675-d175-48cf-ab9d-b0f37b225a63', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', '85e4ae6e-5665-4759-83f3-5e79a2286d1f', $q$Solstice$q$, $q$Y3 Solstice local No$q$, 3, $q$Solstice Onshore Wind - Project execution opportunity$q$, $q$<p>You have the option to utilize local suppliers. They offer lower CAPEX due to local wages, and have experience with 6 MW turbines offering higher energy output. However, the turbines offered have only been used in a very different project.</p><p><br></p><p>Over the project lifetime, the OPEX is expected to be slightly lower. There are potential schedule and integration risks.</p><p><br></p><p>There are two alternative actions:</p>$q$, $q$1. Choose local suppliers. Reduces CAPEX to 1.2 MUSD/MW. Capacity factor is forecasted to increase to 47%.$q$, null, null, null, 0.47, $q$renewable$q$, null, 0, true, null),
  ('69ee800a-90d1-4fbe-a1b5-8f9153921ab6', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', '3d954298-e0c2-4a9f-ad33-dc557f0f74b1', $q$Breeze$q$, $q$2 Community resistance$q$, 3, $q$$q$, $q$$q$, $q$2. Reject demands and proceed with the project as planned. Increases CAPEX with $0.1 M/MW due to high legal costs.$q$, null, null, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('6a2e0f01-fbe5-48dc-b0af-94c95603a3a8', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', 'df6ae15a-a536-442d-b6e8-ee21e8e68341', $q$Nimbus$q$, $q$2Community resistance-Nimbus$q$, 3, $q$$q$, $q$$q$, $q$2. Reject demands and proceed with the project as planned. Increases CAPEX with $0.1 M/MW due to high legal costs.$q$, null, null, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('325646ef-c7ed-4230-bd98-b8a5e122cf15', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', '07fb9c89-3abd-4eba-8fb9-b532912f43a0', $q$Refinery$q$, $q$Y3_1_Refinery more capacity-Refinery$q$, 3, $q$REFINERY - Opportunity to increase production$q$, $q$<p>Exploration activities are rapidly increasing, and forecasts indicate an opportunity to expand capacity by an additional 200 kbpd. This investment is highly encouraged due to strong demand for fuel, gasoline, and feedstock in Exlandia’s petrochemical industry.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>The required investment amounts to 2.4 BUSD, with fixed operating expenses rising to 80 MUSD. By implementing new and upgraded technologies, product prices are projected to increase by 20%.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>You are presented with two options:</p>$q$, $q$1. Proceed with the investment: Expand production capacity to 500 kbpd within three years, capturing the growing demand and strengthening market position.$q$, null, true, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('48f215d0-830b-43ae-8b3b-3ba48460ba94', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', '07fb9c89-3abd-4eba-8fb9-b532912f43a0', $q$Refinery$q$, $q$Y3_2_Refinery maintain capacity-Refinery$q$, 3, $q$$q$, $q$$q$, $q$2. Hold current production levels: Limit production to a maximum of 300 kbpd, risking a loss of market share in the local market.$q$, null, true, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('9123e896-6ea1-4d2e-90d8-3ebe565eeb9a', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', 'b8d9638a-5d81-44bc-8818-fdc85f4f417a', $q$Delphi$q$, $q$Y3_2Find_delphi_offshoreloading-Delphi$q$, 3, $q$$q$, $q$$q$, $q$2. Platform with subsurface storage (SSU) for offshore loading; CAPEX 3120 MUSD, OPEX 305 MUSD.$q$, null, null, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('c596774a-246e-4223-a0e1-00089c2d45f3', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', 'b8d9638a-5d81-44bc-8818-fdc85f4f417a', $q$Delphi$q$, $q$Y3_3Find_delphi_pipelines_to_Fresco_or_helena-Delphi$q$, 3, $q$$q$, $q$$q$, $q$3. Plattform exporting with pipeline to Fresco and/or Helena: CAPEX 2740 MUSD, OPEX 280 MUSD.$q$, null, null, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('59ab5dab-2662-4067-80e6-6741fb8fddb1', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', 'e38e608a-4b65-409d-ab70-be7dc51e5f8f', $q$Aurelia$q$, $q$Y1_1Aurelia_new field design-Aurelia$q$, 3, $q$AURELIA - Subsurface optimization$q$, $q$<p>New seismic interpretation processes with AI suggests an optimized drainage strategy with fewer production wells combined with increased pressure support.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Would you like to optimize this option in parallell? Cost is 30 MUSD.</strong></p>$q$, $q$1. Optimize field design and drainage strategy.$q$, null, true, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
  ('43a303cc-a070-4a7d-a919-e66b769a9bea', '95d38b90-1d15-4c16-99d3-9cfff27f4036', 'a7511f7f-8d0d-4135-898e-78f2b5c72d36', $q$Icarus$q$, $q$1Y4_Icarus_drywells-Icarus$q$, 3, $q$ICARUS - Dry exploration wells$q$, $q$<p>Exploration wells are dry, and probability is reduced to 20%. However, new seismic is promising. </p><p><br></p><p><strong>Choose either to continue with investing 140 MUSD in 2 more exploration wells, or initiate sale of the license.</strong></p>$q$, $q$1. Invest in further exploration, 140 MUSD.$q$, null, true, null, null, null, null, 0, true, null),
